      value: -40
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 847925133356509755, guid: 6ca5b3bf0b1bcab46aa5604ec797bce7, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Size
      value: 6
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 847925133356509755, guid: 6ca5b3bf0b1bcab46aa5604ec797bce7, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: "That\u2019s Correct!\r\n\r\nThe possible outcomes when rolling a fair
        six-sided die are:\r\n\r\n1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\r\n\r\nSince the die is fair,
        **each number has an equal chance of being rolled.\r\n\r\nLet\u2019s define
        the events:\r\n\r\nEvent A: A 2 is rolled\r\nEvent B: A 5 is rolled\r\n\r\nLet\u2019s
        list the possible outcomes:\r\n\r\n1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\n\r\nThere are 6 total
        possible outcomes.\r\n\r\nOut of these, 1 outcome corresponds to Event A
        (rolling a 2) and 1 outcome corresponds to Event B (rolling a 5).\r\n\r\nWe
        can calculate the probability using the formula:\r\n\r\nP(A \\text{ or }
        B) = P(A) + P(B)\r\n\r\n\r\nP(A) = \\frac{1}{6}\r\n\r\nP(B) = \\frac{1}{6}\r\n\r\nP(A
        \\text{ or } B) = \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{6}\r\n\r\nP(A \\text{ or } B)
        = \\frac{2}{6}\r\n\r\nP(A \\text{ or } B) = \\frac{1}{3}\r\n\r\nSo, the probability
        of rolling a 2 or a 5 is ( \\frac{1}{3} ) or about 0.33 (33%).\r\n\r\nThe
        die has two favorable outcomes (2 and 5) out of six possible outcomes, so
        the chance of rolling either number is one-third.\r\n"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
