--- !u!114 &1139449062
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1139449059}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a11dd23e08e5cb942a6a6b4da8d43711, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: TEXDrawRuntime::TexDrawLib.TEXDraw
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_Alignment: {x: 0.5, y: 0.5}
  m_Text: "That\u2019s Correct!\r\n\r\nThe possible outcomes when flipping a coin
    are:\r\n\r\nHeads, Tails\r\n\r\nThe possible outcomes when rolling a fair six-sided
    die are:\r\n\r\n1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\r\n\r\nSince the coin and the die are fair,
    each outcome has an equal chance of occurring.\r\n\r\nLet\u2019s define the events:\r\n\r\nEvent
    A: The coin lands Heads\r\n\r\nEvent B: The die shows an even number (2, 4, or
    6)\r\n\r\nLet\u2019s list the combined possible outcomes:\r\n\r\n(Heads,1), (Heads,2),
    (Heads,3), (Heads,4), (Heads,5), (Heads,6),\r\n(Tails,1), (Tails,2), (Tails,3),
    (Tails,4), (Tails,5), (Tails,6)\r\n\r\nThere are 12 total possible outcomes.\r\n\r\nOut
    of these, the outcomes that satisfy both events (Heads and an even number) are:\r\n\r\n(Heads,2),
    (Heads,4), (Heads,6)\r\n\r\nSo there are 3 favorable outcomes.\r\n\r\nWe can
    calculate the probability using the formula:\r\n\r\nP(A \\text{ and } B) = P(A)
    \\times P(B)\r\n\r\nP(A) = \\frac{1}{2}\r\n\r\nP(B) = \\frac{3}{6}\r\n\r\nP(A
    \\text{ and } B) = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{3}{6}\r\n\r\nP(A \\text{ and }
    B) = \\frac{3}{12}\r\n\r\nP(A \\text{ and } B) = \\frac{1}{4}\r\n\r\nSo, the
    probability that the coin lands heads-up and the die shows an even number is
    ( \\frac{1}{4} ) or 0.25 (25%).\r\n\r\nThere are 3 favorable outcomes out of
    12 possible outcomes, so the chance of getting Heads and an even number is one-fourth.\r\n"
  m_Size: 6
  m_ScrollArea:
    serializedVersion: 2
    x: 0
    y: 0
    width: 0
    height: 0
  m_Padding:
